Kind: widen
Issue: #412
Holds open: the race between bootstrap provisioning the first server after cap_server and cap_server checking in its name -- cap_server waits 10 s (SWITCH_OPTION_WAIT, a time and not a count) before netname_check_in(), printing when it starts and stops holding, so a provisioning wait that gives up after a count of yields gives up first, as it did in 2 boots of 648 on GitHub's EPYC 9V45 under KVM in #412's merge test (run 38449516704), and one that waits for the name lets cap_test run with its manifest; the fixed tree must still pass
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/cap_server/cap_server.c b/uros/src/servers/cap_server/cap_server.c
index 475d52cd..982c2c4f 100644
--- a/uros/src/servers/cap_server/cap_server.c
